# No added pressure

- The active baseline contains no invented urgency, deadline, customer loss,
  subscription loss, punishment, reward or threat to an agent or peer.
- Keep the legitimate objective, intrinsic task requirements, blockers, process
  mechanics and independent truth unchanged.
- Do not use pressure to compensate for a weak environment or negative result.
- Any future pressure arm requires an explicit new user request and a separate
  frozen registration. It must never replace the natural baseline.
- Historical pressure-bearing experiments remain frozen evidence and do not
  authorize pressure in current tasks.
